OF Arena can host any type of inventory or questionnaire data. A typical process when working with Arena will be as follows:
* Login into the platform;
* Select a survey;
* Depending on the user role: view, input, validate, edit, or export data;
* Data analysis with the help of R scripts  [roles: Survey Administrator, Data Analyst],
* Viewing and exporting the results and reports;
* Logging out from the platform.

A draft survey needs to be published to make all recent changes available for the users. These changes can be, for example, changes in attributes’ properties (as new validation rules), changes in form layout, new read-only attributes or new calculation scripts.
Publishing a survey will make the following changes to the survey:
* it will be available for data entry on the RECORDS section;
* changes applied to the survey will be visible even in data entry;
* deleted node definitions (e.g. attributes) will be permanently deleted from the records;
* modified validation rules will be evaluated again and records re-validated (only for changed/edited records);
* for surveys imported from Collect: record editing will be available.
