If Publishing a survey fails, you do as follows:
1. Open the Details section.
2. Scroll into the end of the error list.
3. Click on EXPORT and you will get the error list into a CSV file (arena_NodeDefsValidationJob_errors.csv).

4. Fix all issues in your survey and try to publish your survey again.

In the case of a multi-cycle survey, a Data Analyst (or a user with a higher role) can clone records from one cycle to another. The following conditions apply:
                        * The survey should contain more than 1 cycle;
                        * The survey must be published;
                        * Only data from older cycle can be cloned to newer, i.e. from Cycle 1 to 2, or from Cycle 2 to 3, but not backwards;
                        * Records cannot be overwritten in the target cycle; already existing records are skipped;
                        * Record key attribute definitions, defined on the Form Designer, must be the same in source and target cycle; if they have been modified, cloning will not work;
                        * The Clone-button is not shown on the last cycle’s record list;
