Always before using data import in Arena, take a backup of your survey with data. Read more here.
Arena can import external data from
                                          1. CSV or Excel files;
                                          2. Open Foris Collect / Collect Mobile files;
                                          3. Arena (backup) / Arena Mobile (export) files;

A survey should be published before a data import is possible.
If you are adding new information into the database using CSV or Excel files, import your data by following a top-down method! In the case of the survey structure described in the next chapter, first enter CLUSTER data as new records, then PLOT data with "update existing records", and then similarly "Reference objects", and so on. Data import template files are numbered to make data importing a bit easier.

The ‘Clone chain from another survey’ feature lets a Survey Administrator or Data Analyst copy a complete chain from a survey they have access to into the survey they are currently working on. The clone operation copies:
                                                                     * the chain's properties (name, labels, and description);
                                                                     * all R scripts;
                                                                     * the calculated result variables (analysis attributes) defined in the chain, re-created under the matching entities of the destination survey;
                                                                     * the categories and taxonomies referenced by those calculated variables, so that coded results keep working after the clone.
The cloned chain is created as a new, independent chain in the destination survey - the source chain is left untouched, and the two chains are not kept in sync after cloning.
